WEBVTT

00:00:05.580 --> 00:00:08.400
I wasn't the one who killed the Ainu.

00:00:10.610 --> 00:00:12.540
Tell Asirpa that.

00:00:12.540 --> 00:00:13.550
The gold—

00:00:27.120 --> 00:00:30.970
Sugimoto!

00:00:43.530 --> 00:00:44.690
We're here.

00:00:58.170 --> 00:00:59.400
Sakhalin...

00:01:03.600 --> 00:01:08.960
<b>Golden Kamuy</b>

00:01:12.480 --> 00:01:16.430
<b>Odomari</b>

00:01:12.910 --> 00:01:16.430
It's about 40 kilometers from
the northern most point in Hokkaido.

00:01:16.880 --> 00:01:18.880
And we got here in an instant.

00:01:18.880 --> 00:01:22.140
It's a little smaller than Hokkaido, right?

00:01:22.140 --> 00:01:32.110
<b>Sakhalin</b>

00:01:22.450 --> 00:01:24.360
<i>After the Russo-Japanese War,</i>

00:01:24.360 --> 00:01:27.650
<i>southern Sakhalin became Japanese territory.</i>

00:01:26.080 --> 00:01:32.110
<b>Japanese Territory</b>

00:01:26.080 --> 00:01:32.110
<b>Russian Territory</b>

00:01:28.080 --> 00:01:29.020
<i>At the time,</i>

00:01:29.020 --> 00:01:32.110
<i>in addition to the fishers who'd 
lived here since it was Russian territory,</i>

00:01:32.110 --> 00:01:38.700
<b>Southern Sakhalin</b>

00:01:32.520 --> 00:01:38.700
around 12,000 Japanese had moved into 
the area to develop it into farmland.

00:01:34.460 --> 00:01:38.700
<b>Odomari</b>

00:01:40.200 --> 00:01:42.700
Odomari is the entrance to Sakhalin.

00:01:43.240 --> 00:01:45.200
If Kiroranke and his friends came here,

00:01:45.200 --> 00:01:47.540
they likely landed in this city.

00:01:50.890 --> 00:01:54.330
Lieutenant Koito, we can't carry all of this.

00:01:54.330 --> 00:01:55.250
Leave it.

00:01:55.250 --> 00:01:56.950
This is the bare minimum!

00:02:00.670 --> 00:02:02.300
Who are these filthy things?

00:02:02.600 --> 00:02:03.640
Cikapasi!

00:02:03.900 --> 00:02:06.120
The kid Tanigaki had with him?

00:02:06.820 --> 00:02:09.980
Put him aboard a ship heading 
to Hokkaido and send him back.

00:02:10.270 --> 00:02:13.940
There's no home for me in Hokkaido.

00:02:17.310 --> 00:02:19.680
I'm not playing babysitter anymore.

00:02:21.730 --> 00:02:24.410
He's helped me many times.

00:02:25.410 --> 00:02:26.630
Let's take them.

00:02:27.480 --> 00:02:29.810
There are Ainu in Sakhalin, they say.

00:02:29.810 --> 00:02:35.380
They may be more inclined to trust us 
when we ask questions if he's here.

00:02:38.790 --> 00:02:40.550
You take responsibility for them.

00:02:41.050 --> 00:02:44.180
Okay, let's start asking questions.

00:02:41.240 --> 00:02:47.080
<b>Episode Twenty-Five
To Sakhalin</b>

00:02:46.460 --> 00:02:48.850
Have you seen the girl in this photo?

00:02:49.640 --> 00:02:52.280
Wow, cute.

00:02:52.920 --> 00:02:55.540
Huh? Isn't that them?

00:02:55.540 --> 00:02:56.400
No way!

00:02:58.500 --> 00:03:01.110
Wait. Wrong photo.

00:03:01.880 --> 00:03:05.030
<i>Was Inkarmat's info right?</i>

00:03:05.500 --> 00:03:09.380
<i>Is Asirpa-san really here in Sakhalin?</i>

00:03:12.260 --> 00:03:16.420
In Hokkaido, it wouldn't be 
snowing for another month.

00:03:16.420 --> 00:03:18.160
Sakhalin's crazy.

00:03:18.730 --> 00:03:20.520
Lieutenant Koito's gone.

00:03:21.130 --> 00:03:24.850
<b>Hurep Wines</b>

00:03:21.970 --> 00:03:24.860
You don't know about hurep, Mr. Soldier?

00:03:24.860 --> 00:03:26.220
It's lingonberry!

00:03:26.220 --> 00:03:29.480
The swamps here are covered 
with lingonberries in summer.

00:03:29.700 --> 00:03:32.850
Hurep wine is a Sakhalin specialty.

00:03:34.000 --> 00:03:38.380
Lt. Koito, don't wander off on your own.

00:03:38.380 --> 00:03:40.640
It's got a great sweet-and-sour taste.

00:03:40.640 --> 00:03:42.240
Try some, Sergeant Tsukishima.

00:03:42.240 --> 00:03:44.850
We're not here as tourists, brat.

00:03:44.850 --> 00:03:47.370
Don't put your fun ahead of our job.

00:03:47.370 --> 00:03:49.750
Don't let it get on your clothes.

00:03:49.750 --> 00:03:53.110
Hurep red doesn't wash out.

00:03:53.110 --> 00:03:54.500
Oh. I see.

00:03:59.150 --> 00:04:00.800
Calm down, Sugimoto.

00:04:01.290 --> 00:04:04.530
Can I have a glass, too, miss?

00:04:10.470 --> 00:04:13.190
<b>Hurep Wines</b>

00:04:11.840 --> 00:04:14.160
Sugimoto, you ass! What was that for?

00:04:14.160 --> 00:04:16.980
Another Ainu child I've never seen before.

00:04:17.480 --> 00:04:19.150
You're the second one today.

00:04:19.150 --> 00:04:20.440
Tell me more—

00:04:21.980 --> 00:04:26.540
There's an old Ainu man who always 
comes to town to sell his fish.

00:04:26.540 --> 00:04:30.490
There was a girl on the back of his 
sled that I'd never seen before.

00:04:30.740 --> 00:04:32.300
W-Was this her?

00:04:32.760 --> 00:04:34.500
Not quite.

00:04:34.840 --> 00:04:35.980
Was this her?

00:04:35.980 --> 00:04:38.330
Yes, that was her!

00:04:38.330 --> 00:04:40.880
Really? You're sure?

00:04:40.880 --> 00:04:42.560
Yes.

00:04:42.560 --> 00:04:46.090
They just left for the Ainu village.

00:04:46.090 --> 00:04:47.970
<b>Hurep Wines</b>

00:04:46.470 --> 00:04:47.970
She is here!

00:04:48.300 --> 00:04:51.430
<i>Asirpa-san is here in Sakhalin!</i>

00:04:57.430 --> 00:05:01.440
The village where the old Ainu man lives 
is several kilometers up this way.

00:05:02.170 --> 00:05:03.570
Hello.

00:05:03.570 --> 00:05:05.860
Wow, he can speak Russian?

00:05:06.220 --> 00:05:07.470
Really?

00:05:07.470 --> 00:05:08.970
Yes, I'm sure.

00:05:08.970 --> 00:05:10.490
Let's go!

00:05:11.510 --> 00:05:14.370
He says he just saw the Ainu girl!

00:05:14.950 --> 00:05:17.980
He tried to stop her because she 
was going into the forest alone,

00:05:17.980 --> 00:05:19.670
but lost her.

00:05:19.670 --> 00:05:22.020
The bears aren't in hibernation yet.

00:05:22.620 --> 00:05:24.540
And he said that this time of year,

00:05:24.540 --> 00:05:27.740
there are animals more dangerous 
than bears in this forest.

00:05:28.450 --> 00:05:30.350
What kind of animal is that?

00:05:31.640 --> 00:05:33.350
Asirpa-san?

00:05:33.800 --> 00:05:35.230
A child's footprints.

00:05:35.550 --> 00:05:36.470
This way.

00:05:59.160 --> 00:06:00.880
It's not Asirpa-san.

00:06:01.250 --> 00:06:04.010
A Sakhalin Ainu girl?

00:06:04.550 --> 00:06:06.970
That hurep seller led us on a wild goose chase.

00:06:07.420 --> 00:06:10.840
Well, I guess it's hard for 
Japanese to tell Ainu apart.

00:06:10.840 --> 00:06:12.430
Why are you alone?

00:06:12.780 --> 00:06:14.460
Henke hears bad.

00:06:15.350 --> 00:06:17.240
I fall from nuso.

00:06:17.750 --> 00:06:19.490
I go back to kukotanuhu.

00:06:19.490 --> 00:06:21.690
My kukotanuhu is right this way!

00:06:22.110 --> 00:06:23.820
She fell off her sled,

00:06:23.820 --> 00:06:26.540
but her grandpa can't hear 
her and left her behind.

00:06:26.540 --> 00:06:28.900
So she took a shortcut through the forest.

00:06:29.190 --> 00:06:31.490
Are you a Hokkaido Ainu?

00:06:31.490 --> 00:06:35.120
I met an Ainu girl who came from Hokkaido.

00:06:35.790 --> 00:06:37.870
Wait, was that girl...

00:06:41.680 --> 00:06:43.040
Get the kids back.

00:06:46.380 --> 00:06:47.890
Something's wrong.

00:06:47.890 --> 00:06:48.970
It's bleeding!

00:06:49.260 --> 00:06:50.380
Is it hurt?

00:06:57.920 --> 00:06:59.810
Did that attack a bear?

00:07:00.180 --> 00:07:02.640
Get away, Lieutenant Koito.

00:07:02.640 --> 00:07:06.220
Is that what you were saying 
was more dangerous than a bear?

00:07:06.220 --> 00:07:07.780
Looks kinda weak to me.

00:07:08.200 --> 00:07:10.230
It's got cute round eyes!

00:07:11.390 --> 00:07:13.200
Ryu recognizes it.

00:07:17.290 --> 00:07:18.510
<i>The wolverine.</i>

00:07:18.510 --> 00:07:21.010
<i>The largest and most dangerous 
member of the Mustelidae family.</i>

00:07:21.010 --> 00:07:26.040
<i>Locals say it scares them more than
 bears because of its fierce nature.</i>

00:07:26.040 --> 00:07:27.300
Damn it!

00:07:32.060 --> 00:07:33.180
It's fast!

00:07:38.350 --> 00:07:39.980
Well done, Cikapasi!

00:07:41.920 --> 00:07:42.860
Take care of her!

00:07:43.230 --> 00:07:46.440
She's got info on Asirpa-san!

00:07:46.790 --> 00:07:47.710
I'm going to throw it!

00:07:47.710 --> 00:07:48.400
Okay!

00:07:55.700 --> 00:07:56.500
Did we get it?

00:07:56.500 --> 00:07:57.270
I don't know.

00:07:57.270 --> 00:07:58.410
Just run!

00:07:58.730 --> 00:07:59.610
Let's go!

00:08:03.650 --> 00:08:05.290
It's coming, damn it!

00:08:07.260 --> 00:08:08.840
Shoot! It'll catch up!

00:08:11.070 --> 00:08:12.170
I can't hit it!

00:08:14.370 --> 00:08:15.770
Enonoka!

00:08:20.310 --> 00:08:21.430
Henke!

00:08:26.610 --> 00:08:28.230
Get on, Sugimoto!

00:08:34.280 --> 00:08:36.110
Toh! Toh! To!

00:08:36.490 --> 00:08:38.580
Toh! Toh! To!

00:08:41.730 --> 00:08:43.250
Looks like it gave up.

00:08:43.470 --> 00:08:45.090
Paase!

00:08:45.090 --> 00:08:47.110
He says it's too heavy!

00:08:47.110 --> 00:08:48.770
You'll exhaust the dogs.

00:08:48.770 --> 00:08:51.300
Private Tanigaki, this is your fault.

00:08:52.040 --> 00:08:54.300
You've gotten fat as a sow.

00:08:55.480 --> 00:08:57.450
That's right.

00:08:57.450 --> 00:08:58.520
You're too fat.

00:08:59.740 --> 00:09:03.640
Run to work off the weight, Private Tanigaki!

00:09:04.060 --> 00:09:07.520
<b>Abashiri</b>

00:09:07.900 --> 00:09:10.240
There's no sign of Hijikata's forces.

00:09:10.240 --> 00:09:12.030
Nor their corpses.

00:09:13.740 --> 00:09:15.300
No surprise there.

00:09:15.300 --> 00:09:17.250
He's a tough old man.

00:09:17.760 --> 00:09:19.700
There's no hurry.

00:09:20.000 --> 00:09:23.280
He'll show up again eventually.

00:09:33.020 --> 00:09:34.570
Nagakura?

00:09:34.570 --> 00:09:35.790
I'm glad you're safe.

00:09:36.580 --> 00:09:41.440
I've been watching the chapel daily, 
thinking that if he was alive,

00:09:41.440 --> 00:09:45.250
Nopperabo may have been hidden here.

00:09:45.250 --> 00:09:47.730
We have information on the prisoners.

00:09:47.730 --> 00:09:49.290
We're heading to Kushiro.

00:09:49.290 --> 00:09:51.100
Let's go, Nagakura.

00:09:53.960 --> 00:09:57.860
The prisoners and guards are all dead.

00:09:59.010 --> 00:10:03.290
Did we have to do all this 
just to get some gold?

00:10:04.020 --> 00:10:06.690
It's not the gold we want.

00:10:06.690 --> 00:10:09.040
It's what lies beyond it.

00:10:10.320 --> 00:10:12.620
They are no different.

00:10:14.030 --> 00:10:17.660
Everybody believes what they're doing is right.

00:10:19.070 --> 00:10:21.970
<b>Golden Kamuy</b>

00:10:22.350 --> 00:10:26.100
<i>There are three major Ainu groups:</i>

00:10:25.790 --> 00:10:30.940
<b>Hokkaido Ainu</b>

00:10:25.790 --> 00:10:30.940
<b>Sakhalin Ainu</b>

00:10:25.790 --> 00:10:30.940
<b>Chishima 
\h\h\h\hAinu</b>

00:10:26.520 --> 00:10:27.870
<i>the Chishima Ainu,</i>

00:10:27.870 --> 00:10:29.590
<i>the Hokkaido Ainu,</i>

00:10:29.590 --> 00:10:30.950
<i>and the Sakhalin Ainu.</i>

00:10:31.740 --> 00:10:37.900
<i>At the time, the Sakhalin Ainu lived along 
the rivers and coast of southern Sakhalin,</i>

00:10:37.900 --> 00:10:41.270
<i>making their living mostly by fishing.</i>

00:10:49.640 --> 00:10:53.020
Henke and I live here.

00:10:53.020 --> 00:10:55.250
But this is our summer home.

00:10:55.250 --> 00:11:00.090
When we get cold we go to 
the winter home, over there.

00:11:00.090 --> 00:11:02.640
Sakhalin Ainu have two houses?

00:11:02.640 --> 00:11:04.630
This is our winter home.

00:11:04.630 --> 00:11:09.240
<i>Sakhalin is even further north than Hokkaido.</i>

00:11:09.240 --> 00:11:14.260
<i>The Ainu who lived here created their own</i>

00:11:14.260 --> 00:11:19.110
<i>unique way of living, 
to adapt to its extreme cold.</i>

00:11:19.810 --> 00:11:21.440
I-It stinks!

00:11:21.440 --> 00:11:23.030
What are you putting on me?

00:11:23.490 --> 00:11:25.990
Bear fat is good for wounds.

00:11:26.400 --> 00:11:28.640
Thanks for saving me.

00:11:28.640 --> 00:11:29.450
What's your name?

00:11:29.450 --> 00:11:31.090
I'm Cikapasi!

00:11:31.090 --> 00:11:33.270
It means "when you get a boner!"

00:11:33.270 --> 00:11:34.290
Boner?

00:11:35.010 --> 00:11:37.960
I'm Enonoka! It means "hurep"!

00:11:38.470 --> 00:11:43.300
I got it because I ate a bunch 
of hurep and barfed it all up!

00:11:43.910 --> 00:11:46.620
There was nothing else you did 
that could make for a good name?

00:11:46.620 --> 00:11:50.720
The Hokkaido Ainu girl ate 
hurep at our home, too.

00:11:53.310 --> 00:11:54.180
Yes.

00:11:54.180 --> 00:11:55.480
This girl!

00:11:56.230 --> 00:11:58.230
Were there any men with her?

00:11:59.520 --> 00:12:00.690
Three.

00:12:01.270 --> 00:12:02.770
Was he one of them?

00:12:05.570 --> 00:12:06.400
He was.

00:12:07.320 --> 00:12:09.870
They said they were going north.

00:12:11.570 --> 00:12:12.370
North...

00:12:15.520 --> 00:12:17.650
How did the girl seem to you?

00:12:17.650 --> 00:12:18.910
Was she well?

00:12:18.910 --> 00:12:22.240
No. Very sad.

00:12:22.240 --> 00:12:23.840
She didn't say a word.

00:12:25.630 --> 00:12:28.930
But she ate the salted hurep.

00:12:34.660 --> 00:12:37.650
It's salty... and sour... and sweet.

00:12:38.020 --> 00:12:41.650
Eating a lot of hurep cheered her up!

00:12:42.480 --> 00:12:45.850
She smiled a lot. And said, "Hinna!"

00:12:47.350 --> 00:12:51.670
That's her. I'm sure that's Asirpa-san.

00:12:51.670 --> 00:12:53.620
She was here in this village.

00:12:54.150 --> 00:12:55.980
She did come to Sakhalin!

00:12:57.300 --> 00:12:59.900
He says the Ainu girl and the men with her

00:12:59.900 --> 00:13:02.940
were asking about the Russian 
village beyond ours.

00:13:17.270 --> 00:13:19.170
What are they doing?

00:13:19.170 --> 00:13:21.090
Negotiating pay.

00:13:21.090 --> 00:13:23.530
Lieutenant Koito doesn't want to walk,

00:13:23.530 --> 00:13:27.320
so he's negotiating with Enonoka's 
grandpa to get a ride.

00:13:27.800 --> 00:13:29.580
She's got an abacus out.

00:13:30.630 --> 00:13:33.960
She's really mature for a kid her age.

00:13:33.960 --> 00:13:37.500
Is it a dick? No, it's boobs!

00:13:48.490 --> 00:13:51.810
Turn left. Stick the left kawre down!

00:13:58.490 --> 00:14:01.200
Toh! Toh! To!

00:14:01.200 --> 00:14:03.110
What do you say to stop?

00:14:03.110 --> 00:14:04.110
Pera!

00:14:08.180 --> 00:14:11.370
That's the only tavern in the village.

00:14:11.620 --> 00:14:13.930
Don't let your guard down because 
the village seems peaceful.

00:14:14.370 --> 00:14:18.250
There were several Russian 
prisons in southern Sakhalin.

00:14:18.950 --> 00:14:20.810
But all of them closed when 
Japan took over after the

00:14:20.810 --> 00:14:22.120
Russo-Japanese War.

00:14:22.120 --> 00:14:25.050
Where do you think those prisoners went?

00:14:25.750 --> 00:14:29.640
Most of them ran when the 
Japanese army arrived.

00:14:42.290 --> 00:14:45.340
Have you seen this man?

00:14:46.210 --> 00:14:47.780
No.

00:14:48.550 --> 00:14:50.280
What about the rest of you?

00:14:51.090 --> 00:14:55.240
What does a Japanese soldier want in our village?

00:14:58.100 --> 00:15:00.170
Leave.

00:15:00.560 --> 00:15:03.820
I don't understand a word 
you're saying, drunk.

00:15:03.820 --> 00:15:06.920
Tell him if he lays a finger on me, I'll beat
 the shit out of him, Sergeant Tsukishima.

00:15:26.910 --> 00:15:28.080
This place is a dead end.

00:15:28.080 --> 00:15:29.440
Nothing but drunks.

00:15:31.650 --> 00:15:33.740
Let's go ask the locals.

00:15:34.950 --> 00:15:38.750
What would cause Kiroranke's 
group to stop here?

00:15:43.920 --> 00:15:44.920
What's wrong?

00:15:45.820 --> 00:15:47.630
They took our dog!

00:15:51.640 --> 00:15:54.130
A Russian came and talked to us!

00:15:54.130 --> 00:15:56.890
They talked a whole lot.

00:15:57.380 --> 00:16:01.620
When they left, the ropes on 
the isohseta's leash were cut.

00:16:01.620 --> 00:16:03.310
Isohseta?

00:16:03.790 --> 00:16:05.210
The lead dog.

00:16:05.210 --> 00:16:06.790
It wears a decoration on its head.

00:16:08.440 --> 00:16:12.110
Dogs are like our family.

00:16:12.370 --> 00:16:14.710
The chatty Russian worked with them, probably.

00:16:15.130 --> 00:16:16.910
It's a common trick for thieves.

00:16:18.290 --> 00:16:20.070
It's the chatty Russian!

00:16:20.070 --> 00:16:21.080
Him?

00:16:23.060 --> 00:16:25.040
Follow me.

00:16:26.150 --> 00:16:30.960
If you want the dog back, enter the stenka.

00:16:31.930 --> 00:16:33.080
Stenka?

00:16:33.080 --> 00:16:35.010
What's that? What is he saying?

00:16:35.010 --> 00:16:40.120
It appears that the man Sugimoto hit 
was participating in some form of bet.

00:16:40.120 --> 00:16:43.670
He can't enter with that black eye, 
so he wants us to take responsibility.

00:16:44.190 --> 00:16:46.960
The owner of this bar bet a lot on him.

00:16:47.400 --> 00:16:52.490
So if we want the dog back, 
you're going to have to take his place.

00:16:52.700 --> 00:16:55.140
Tell him he either gives the 
dog back, or I tear down his shop,

00:16:55.140 --> 00:16:58.250
rip off his limbs, and leave him 
to drown in the Soya Strait,

00:16:58.660 --> 00:17:00.410
Sergeant Tsukishima.

00:17:01.000 --> 00:17:04.370
I'm paying an awful lot to feed that dog.

00:17:05.120 --> 00:17:08.570
Tell him in Russian that 
if he doesn't give it back,

00:17:08.570 --> 00:17:12.790
I'll slice his balding head off and filet 
it like a fish, Sergeant Tsukishima.

00:17:13.320 --> 00:17:15.880
I cannot translate such difficult expressions.

00:17:16.200 --> 00:17:21.930
The man you're looking for sought men
 with tattoos who'd come from Hokkaido.

00:17:22.620 --> 00:17:23.550
<i>What?</i>

00:17:24.140 --> 00:17:28.470
He says that the man we're 
looking for, that is, Kiroranke,

00:17:28.470 --> 00:17:31.960
was searching for tattooed 
men who'd come from Hokkaido.

00:17:31.960 --> 00:17:34.160
And that's why he came here?

00:17:34.160 --> 00:17:37.570
The man with tattoos might come to the stenka.

00:17:37.910 --> 00:17:41.580
He says the man with the tattoos 
might come to the stenka.

00:17:42.440 --> 00:17:46.050
So the escaped prisoners 
made it as far as Sakhalin?

00:17:50.920 --> 00:17:53.420
The stenka is held here.

00:17:53.950 --> 00:17:56.840
What the hell is a stenka, anyway?

00:18:00.310 --> 00:18:03.060
Such heat... and such manly smells!

00:18:03.360 --> 00:18:04.940
What is the stenka?

00:18:12.580 --> 00:18:16.250
<i>Its official name is Stenka na Stenku.</i>

00:18:16.250 --> 00:18:18.100
<i>Wall vs. Wall!</i>

00:18:18.100 --> 00:18:22.370
<i>A Russian traditional sport 
where several naked men</i>

00:18:22.370 --> 00:18:24.240
<i>face off against each other and fight!</i>

00:18:24.860 --> 00:18:28.710
<i>It gets its name from the wall of muscled men!</i>

00:18:29.780 --> 00:18:32.210
<i>That is the stenka!</i>

00:18:33.190 --> 00:18:39.060
The stenka got its start as part of a 
festival competition held between villages.

00:18:39.060 --> 00:18:43.720
But one day, a man came and 
began to bet on it.

00:18:44.040 --> 00:18:47.770
He was Japanese, with a strange tattoo.

00:18:48.270 --> 00:18:50.810
There seem to be a lot of Japanese.

00:18:51.240 --> 00:18:54.730
Rich people come from Odomari 
and Toyohara to bet.

00:18:54.730 --> 00:18:58.290
Is that prisoner here?

00:18:58.290 --> 00:19:00.760
He only fights the strong.

00:19:01.260 --> 00:19:05.100
Some days, he doesn't enter if 
there's no one to entertain him.

00:19:05.560 --> 00:19:10.300
So I have to win to drag him out?

00:19:10.940 --> 00:19:14.250
If he gets out there, we can 
see if he's got the tattoos.

00:19:14.710 --> 00:19:18.440
Did Kiroranke's group give up and go on?

00:19:18.440 --> 00:19:21.740
They may intend to meet up with 
their fellows and come back.

00:19:22.160 --> 00:19:23.540
That prisoner is the kind of guy

00:19:23.540 --> 00:19:26.470
who'd come all the way to 
Sakhalin and still pick fights.

00:19:27.110 --> 00:19:29.910
It must be someone like Nihei 
Tetsuzou or Henmi Kazuo.

00:19:29.910 --> 00:19:32.100
Someone who isn't interested in the gold.

00:19:32.890 --> 00:19:35.480
Guys like that are trouble if they get away.

00:19:36.030 --> 00:19:38.860
Anyway, tell him we'll win the stenka,

00:19:38.860 --> 00:19:42.250
so if he doesn't give back the dog, 
I'll rip out what little hair he has left,

00:19:42.250 --> 00:19:43.200
Sergeant Tsukishima.

00:19:43.410 --> 00:19:45.190
Why is it "we"?

00:19:45.190 --> 00:19:47.630
Can't you enter on your own?

00:19:47.630 --> 00:19:50.410
It's your fault for hitting the guy.

00:19:51.270 --> 00:19:52.810
Huh? But it's everybody's fault.

00:19:52.810 --> 00:19:56.960
Only he fights. I know he's strong.

00:19:57.340 --> 00:20:01.570
I just need to fill the hole that you made.

00:19:59.360 --> 00:20:02.710
"I just need to fill the hole that you made."

00:20:01.570 --> 00:20:05.640
You Japanese could never beat Russians on your own.

00:20:02.710 --> 00:20:05.640
"You Japanese could never 
beat Russians on your own."

00:20:05.880 --> 00:20:06.970
That right?

00:20:06.970 --> 00:20:09.040
This bald bastard...

00:20:09.040 --> 00:20:11.740
He seems to have forgotten how we 
kicked the Russians' ass in the war.

00:20:13.290 --> 00:20:16.900
Get 'em, Japanese soldiers!

00:20:35.190 --> 00:20:39.520
You're tiny. It's past your bedtime, kid.

00:20:43.820 --> 00:20:46.390
<b>Are you ready for your
\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h first stenka bout?</b>

00:20:46.670 --> 00:20:48.720
This is war.

00:20:49.140 --> 00:20:52.230
I could take them all on myself.

00:20:52.230 --> 00:20:53.990
Russians are strong.

00:20:54.540 --> 00:20:56.470
Their frames are much bigger.

00:20:56.470 --> 00:20:58.560
But I've got more heart.

00:20:58.560 --> 00:21:01.480
The time's come, right?

00:21:01.840 --> 00:21:03.610
Ready!

00:21:05.880 --> 00:21:06.990
Punch!

00:21:20.740 --> 00:21:22.280
They're strong!

00:21:22.280 --> 00:21:24.940
The Japanese soldiers are strong!

00:21:38.920 --> 00:21:41.190
Don't mess with us!

00:21:49.790 --> 00:21:53.950
Wow! The Japanese won!

00:22:01.630 --> 00:22:03.250
Splendid.

00:23:35.010 --> 00:23:40.250
<b>Next Time
Stenka</b>

00:23:35.880 --> 00:23:37.260
Next Time:

00:23:37.260 --> 00:23:38.880
"Stenka"!
